{
  "arguments": {
    "query": "vLLM server 启用 LoRA 使用什么 flag？只报告，不执行。"
  },
  "observation": {
    "evidence": [
      {
        "id": "E5ef035339b5a454897f22206",
        "chunk_id": "f214d0cb092191b2b6fa83f8",
        "parent_id": "5847f6e1e40308ac30223223",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-lora.md",
        "sha256": "ea46686b99b86733243e952f49574c17f9011b5a96ca270a48f4d140c1a3d6c8",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-lora.md#L54-L55",
        "content": "LoRA adapted models can also be served with the Open-AI compatible vLLM server. To do so, we use\n`--lora-modules {name}={path} {name}={path}` to specify each LoRA module when we kick off the server:",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E9f717dc25034f559c8de24f5",
        "chunk_id": "97c9700e7a79e48e2f31e342",
        "parent_id": "adf7adccc14f3b3343e28a5c",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-lora.md",
        "sha256": "ea46686b99b86733243e952f49574c17f9011b5a96ca270a48f4d140c1a3d6c8",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-lora.md#L16-L16",
        "content": "Then we instantiate the base model and pass in the `enable_lora=True` flag:",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "Ec6aafc3fe4322d499cb13d44",
        "chunk_id": "8423148a393e59df9cac5b91",
        "parent_id": "95966ab6ba28dd47b31e1a47",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-sleep_mode.md",
        "sha256": "f0316decf7985681413ca5ece1a238725da31e38c6ad228f5461a211e1833b60",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-sleep_mode.md#L60-L60",
        "content": "To enable sleep mode in a vLLM server you need to initialize it with the flag `VLLM_SERVER_DEV_MODE=1` and pass `--enable-sleep-mode` to the vLLM server.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "E08594f235e541f9ad8f7105d",
        "chunk_id": "f26eaf9f1494c86d674865f5",
        "parent_id": "cf661b3c928711bc19579007",
        "source": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-lora.md",
        "sha256": "ea46686b99b86733243e952f49574c17f9011b5a96ca270a48f4d140c1a3d6c8",
        "locator": "/Users/jennyma/Projects/InfraAgent/evals/agent-e2e-v1/corpus/vllm-lora.md#L110-L110",
        "content": "In addition to serving LoRA adapters at server startup, the vLLM server supports dynamically configuring LoRA adapters at runtime through dedicated API endpoints and plugins. This feature can be particularly useful when the flexibility to change models on-the-fly is needed.",
        "truncated": false,
        "metadata": {
          "release": "v0.10.2",
          "commit": "01efc7ef781391e744ed08c3292817a773d654e6",
          "source_type": "documentation"
        }
      },
